    "body": "This is a follow-up to [#35728](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/35728#issuecomment-6214014188). \n\nWhile reviewing that PR, I noticed that `FindTx()` could return `nullopt` even when LevelDB had encountered an error. I first confirmed that a transaction could be retrieved, then deliberately damaged part of the test’s temporary txindex database. LevelDB detected the corruption, but the same lookup returned `nullopt` instead of throwing. Restoring the original data made the lookup work again.\n\nThe candidate scan checks whether the iterator has a valid entry, but it does not check its error status. An invalid iterator can mean that the scan reached the end normally, or that it stopped because of a database error. This means a failed scan can be treated as an ordinary missing transaction.\n\nThis adds `CDBIterator::CheckStatus()` and calls it after the candidate scan, before choosing a result. Any iterator error goes through the existing `HandleError()` path and throws `dbwrapper_error`. A normal missing transaction still returns `nullopt`.",
